WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.786
Stage eleven: three voices, one decision.

2
00:00:05.636 --> 00:00:11.766
Tuesday morning: Camille's threshold session becomes forty-five minutes of easy running.

3
00:00:11.866 --> 00:00:16.532
The measurements, the verdict, the file: that's the substance.

4
00:00:16.632 --> 00:00:23.482
Now, the delivery. Four voices: encouraging, challenging, sober, pedagogue.

5
00:00:24.332 --> 00:00:29.430
The encouraging voice: “Your body is asking for a little breathing room.”

6
00:00:29.530 --> 00:00:33.356
The challenging voice: “What is eating your nights this week?”

7
00:00:33.456 --> 00:00:38.434
The sober voice: verdict first, then a table. Nothing else.

8
00:00:38.534 --> 00:00:42.888
Three tones. And the banner on top hasn't moved a pixel.

9
00:00:43.738 --> 00:00:50.708
Intensity sets firmness: gentle proposes, balanced recommends, strong decides.

10
00:00:50.808 --> 00:00:59.290
Verbosity sets length: brief, three lines; standard, a paragraph; detailed, the full reasoning.

11
00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:03.408
Three lines of configuration. The verdict doesn't move.

12
00:01:04.258 --> 00:01:08.972
And what an identifier can't say? Your profile's “Coaching preferences”.

13
00:01:09.072 --> 00:01:14.170
What motivates you, what doesn't work, what to avoid. It overrides the catalogue.

14
00:01:14.270 --> 00:01:20.304
Camille banned hollow cheers: that sentence disappears. The verdict never does.

15
00:01:21.154 --> 00:01:26.132
Catalogue rule number seven: style never changes the substance.

16
00:01:26.232 --> 00:01:31.978
A workout cancelled for medical reasons stays cancelled, encouraging or challenging.

17
00:01:32.078 --> 00:01:35.112
Tone decides the wording. Never the verdict.

18
00:01:37.662 --> 00:01:42.352
To go further: the “Configuration” page of the documentation.
